  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">N HONDURAS IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will strengthen the capacity of two local institutions and partner with one municipal government to conserve a total of 185,000 acres of forested habitat in and around Pico Bonito National Park (PBNP), as well as the corridor connecting PBNP with the Texiguat Wildlife Refuge and Cuero y Salado National Park in northern Honduras. These forests are critical to diverse neotropical migratory bird species. The project also involves the reforestation of 3,700 acres. Birds that will benefit include the swallow-tailed kite, peregrine falcon, Canada warbler, yellow-billed cuckoo, Kentucky warbler, cerulean warbler, and painted bunting, as well as the endemic Honduran emerald hummingbird.</narrative>
  </description>
